further:
  - slug: mari-syria
    why: Ebla's main commercial rival, and the other side of the hundred years'
      war that runs through the archive period — from Saʿumu's conquests to
      the battle near Terqa.
  - slug: akkadian-empire
    why: Sargon and Naram-Sin both claimed to have destroyed a town called Ibla,
      which is one of the standing hypotheses for Ebla's first destruction.
  - slug: kish-sumer
    why: Gelb placed Ebla within the Kish civilization, and most of Ebla's
      river-boat trade was directed chiefly at Kish.
