[[ ^5 ]]: [[ Michael Astour ]] argues that using the chronology accepted by Pettinato, one obtains the date of 2500 BC for the reign of [[ Ur-Nanshe ]] of [[ Lagash ]], who ruled approximately 150 years prior to Lagash's destruction at the hands of king [[ Lugalzagesi ]]. Since Ur-Nanshe ruled in 2500 BC, and his reign is separated by at least 150 years from Hidar of Mari's reign which saw Ebla's destruction, then the date for that event is pulled beyond 2500 BC and even 2400 BC.

